  "id": "Compound::DB01206 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Lomustine, a member of the alkylating activity class of compounds, is linked to Cyp3a4 through its inclusion in the Alkylating Activity category, which includes Temozolomide, Trabectedin, and Ifosfamide. These compounds all bind to Cyp3a4, suggesting a shared mechanism of interaction with the cytochrome P450 3A4 enzyme. The lowest common ancestors of Lomustine and its included compounds point to broader categories like Antineoplastic Alkylating Agent and Primary Amide, indicating a common structural or functional framework. The evidence suggests that Lomustine may interact with Cyp3a4 through a mechanism involving its alkylating properties, potentially modulating enzyme activity. While the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear, the consistent binding of related compounds to Cyp3a4 implies a possible role for Lomustine in regulating Cyp3a4 function, possibly through indirect mechanisms involving its alkylating activity.",
